# AbarVa — Cursor Rules (Strategic Moves + Programs)

## Visual reference (binding)

Canonical reference: `docs/design/strategic-moves/`

- `tokens.css` — single source of truth for colors, type, spacing, radius, motion. Never introduce new tokens. Never change committed token values.
- `14-strategic-moves-home.html` — high-fidelity prototype (`#dashboard-view`, `#detail-view`, `#originate-view`). Pixel-match layout when implementing.
- `README.md` — implementation brief (acceptance checklist at end).
- `INTEGRATION.md` — what to touch, what to leave alone; **`--gold` → `--abarva-signal-blue`** (never add `--gold` to `tokens.css`).

## Token discipline

- Use only tokens from `tokens.css` (brand + canon).
- No new colors, fonts, radius values, gradients, decorative SVG icons, emoji, or stock illustration.

## Type ramp

- Display headings: Fraunces 500/700 (`--abarva-serif`).
- UI body: Inter 400/500/600 (`--abarva-sans`).
- Mono eyebrows / labels / code: JetBrains Mono 600 (`--abarva-mono`), uppercase, `letter-spacing: 0.12em`. Do not replace mono eyebrows with sans-serif uppercase.

## Surfaces

- Public/marketing/investor: paper `#faf7f1`, navy ink `#0c1a3a`, signal blue accent `#0066CC`.
- Authenticated app (Strategic Moves): cream `--canon-bg-cream`, white cards, ink text. Red/amber/teal are **semantic only**, never decorative.

## Naming doctrine

- User-facing: "Strategic Move" / "Move" / "your moves".
- Internal: `engagements`, `program_*` — **no DB table renames**.
- Routes: `/strategic-moves`, `/strategic-moves/[moveId]`, `/strategic-moves/new`.
- APIs: `/api/v1/programs/*`, `programId`, `getProgramById`, etc. stay.
- Rule: user-visible strings → Move vocabulary; developer-facing → keep program/engagement names.

## Phase labels

- Use `src/lib/programs/phase-labels.ts` (`getPhaseLabel`, `PHASE_LABELS`) for all user-visible phase text. Never duplicate inline maps.

## Phase rail component

- Shared: `src/components/strategic-moves/PhaseRail.tsx` — `<PhaseRail current={n} totalPhases={8} />`. Reuse on Detail, Originate, future surfaces. Do not inline duplicate rails.

## Hard “do not”

- Do not ship the prototype **tweaks** panel to production.
- Do not add `--gold` to `tokens.css`.
- Do not use signal-blue as the in-app **primary** CTA (use ink-on-cream). Signal blue: public surfaces + one accent per page.
- Do not gate edit rights on “participant on move”; any `tenant_member` may edit any move (locked product decision).
- Do not bypass app-layer **`client_id` / tenant** filters on Strategic Moves data paths.
